From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 08:17:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: let a release build emit renderer debug output

VREND_DEBUG_ENABLED was the build's assert configuration, so every
VREND_DEBUG/VREND_DEBUG_EXT site compiled to nothing in a release build and
vrend_init_debug_flags() was never reached. The product builds virglrenderer
with --buildtype release, which meson's b_ndebug=if-release turns into NDEBUG,
so setting VREND_DEBUG together with VIRGL_LOG_LEVEL=debug and VIRGL_LOG_FILE
produced a log with no renderer debug output at all, and the shader, streamout
and command dumps were unavailable exactly where the driver has to be
diagnosed.

Test one global instead. It stays false until vrend_init_debug_flags() finds
at least one flag in VREND_DEBUG, and the guest override needs such a flag as
well, so a run without VREND_DEBUG keeps the same behaviour, the same log
level and the same branch at each site. Initialization no longer hides behind
the macro it is supposed to arm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_debug.c    |  7 ++++++-
 src/vrend/vrend_debug.h    | 13 ++++++++-----
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c |  4 +---
 3 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_debug.c b/src/vrend/vrend_debug.c
index 7606e195db2677b516c3ec19b9d4008dd4319e0d..9093886ccf5d8f3715177687040264abbf355c61 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_debug.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_debug.c
@@ -173,6 +173,8 @@ static const struct debug_named_value vrend_debug_options[] = {
 static uint64_t vrend_debug_flags = 0;
 static int vrend_debug_flags_initalized = 0;
 
+bool vrend_debug_enabled = false;
+
 int vrend_get_debug_flags(const char *flagstring)
 {
    int retval;
@@ -197,8 +199,10 @@ void vrend_init_debug_flags(void)
       vrend_debug_flags_initalized = 1;
       vrend_debug_flags = debug_get_flags_option("VREND_DEBUG",
                                                  vrend_debug_options, 0);
-      if (vrend_debug_flags)
+      if (vrend_debug_flags) {
+         vrend_debug_enabled = true;
          virgl_override_log_level(VIRGL_LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG);
+      }
    }
 }
 
@@ -210,6 +214,7 @@ unsigned vrend_debug(const struct vrend_context *ctx, enum virgl_debug_flags fla
 void vrend_debug_add_flag(enum virgl_debug_flags flag)
 {
    vrend_debug_flags |= flag;
+   vrend_debug_enabled = true;
 }
 
 int  vrend_debug_can_override(void)
diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_debug.h b/src/vrend/vrend_debug.h
index 86288cb87213521b65c9ab69097209cd2de0ed09..bcec83586480dc30cb037fb023bcb7cf9b55ae70 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_debug.h
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_debug.h
@@ -73,11 +73,14 @@ unsigned vrend_debug(const struct vrend_context *ctx, enum virgl_debug_flags fla
 
 void vrend_debug_add_flag(enum virgl_debug_flags flag);
 
-#ifdef NDEBUG
-#define VREND_DEBUG_ENABLED (false)
-#else
-#define VREND_DEBUG_ENABLED (true)
-#endif
+/* Every debug site tests this one global instead of the build's assert
+ * configuration, so a release build can still be asked for renderer debug
+ * output. It stays false until VREND_DEBUG selects at least one flag, and a
+ * guest override needs such a flag as well, so a run without VREND_DEBUG
+ * behaves exactly as a build with the sites compiled out. */
+extern bool vrend_debug_enabled;
+
+#define VREND_DEBUG_ENABLED (vrend_debug_enabled)
 
 #define VREND_DEBUG(flag, ctx,  ...) \
    if (VREND_DEBUG_ENABLED && vrend_debug(ctx, flag)) \
diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index c3de7629e9eb15f64e4bed92f163a3e0a8577ff8..d37273d63b85e55c0615f1ea787faee596053fa6 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -7728,9 +7728,7 @@ int vrend_renderer_init(const struct vrend_if_cbs *cbs, uint32_t flags)
          vrend_state.max_texture_3d_size =
          vrend_state.max_texture_cube_size = 16384;
 
-   if (VREND_DEBUG_ENABLED) {
-      vrend_init_debug_flags();
-   }
+   vrend_init_debug_flags();
 
    ctx_params.shared = false;
    if (flags & VREND_USE_COMPAT_CONTEXT) {
